id: design.retry-idempotency
kind: design
title: pairing retries with idempotency
aliases: retry idempotency, retry safety, retry and idempotency
tags: design, retries, resilience, correctness
questions:
  - when is a retry safe?
  - how do you avoid doing a write twice?
invariant: A retry is safe only where the operation is idempotent; pairing retries with idempotency, not with "it might work," is what prevents duplicate side effects.
answer_30s: Make each retryable operation idempotent first (a client token, a conditional write, a dedupe key), then retry only on the transient causes you can name; retry on a non-idempotent operation and you may double-write, which is worse than not retrying.
when_to_use:
  - any call you will retry
  - external writes, payment calls, state mutations
avoid_when:
  - the operation cannot be made idempotent and the cost of a duplicate matters
related:
  - design.idempotency
  - design.retry-backoff
  - design.circuit-breaker
sources:
  - https://sre.google/sre-book/
